API lookups only find streams that exist, for go2rtc v1.9.15 (7c05066).
Upstream's streams.GetOrPatch, behind api/frame.jpeg, api/stream.mjpeg, api/stream.mp4,
api/stream.m3u8 and every api/ws handler (webrtc, mse, mp4, hls, mjpeg), created a stream from a
src URL, or set an existing stream's source from src with name=: any client that reaches the API
could point a camera's stream at its own producer (GET /api/frame.jpeg?src=rtsp://host/x&name=cam)
or make go2rtc dial any host. GetOrPatch now only returns the stream named by src. The HTTP and
WebSocket pushes into a stream (POST api/stream.mjpeg?dst=, WHIP POST api/webrtc?dst=, api/ws?dst=,
and WHEP POST api/webrtc?src= with an offer that sends video, which upstream's ExchangeSDP turned
into a producer) are refused with 403 (streams.ErrPushDisabled), so a client cannot add its own
producer either. A WebSocket offer's own ice_servers are ignored: only the config's ICE servers
are used, so a client cannot make go2rtc send STUN or TURN to any host. Config streams, ffmpeg:
loopback sources and RTSP publishing (which authenticates on a public listener) are unchanged;
the other pushes (api/stream.ts, api/stream.flv, api/stream, hass) sit on paths app.py never
allows. Comes with its own tests (go test ./internal/streams/ ./internal/mjpeg/ ./internal/webrtc/).

